# A permission to cast spells as though they had flash is judged on the spell the card would be on the stack, under its
# caster, with the continuous effects that would apply to it there (CR 601.2a, 601.3b, 601.3e), not on the card where it
# is. Bot1 controls Arcane Adaptation naming Spirit ("The same is true for creature spells you control"), Rattlechains
# ("You may cast Spirit spells as though they had flash") and Dauthi Voidwalker. Bot2's Llanowar Elves, discarded to
# Faithless Looting, is exiled with a void counter; in Bot2's turn Bot1 sacrifices the Voidwalker to choose it. In Bot2's
# exile, owned by Bot2, the Elves is no Spirit; as Bot1's creature spell it is one (CR 611.3a), so Bot1 casts it in Bot2's
# turn (CR 702.8a), and it enters a Spirit. Its control, with Bot1's own Spirit of the Labyrinth in place of the Elves, is
# rattlechains-lets-its-controller-flash-spirit-spells-and-targets-an-opponents-spirit.

